      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The memory in which it says is NOT storage and is rather RAM. This seems to be a fault of how words are used.\n\nWhat is happening to you is what happens to most users on Quest 2, the game loads so much it fills the RAM, causing the Quest to panic and kill the process like any other Android device. Other times, VRChat will do the panicking for the Quest and send you to your home world.\n\nTo prevent this, I suggest closing any background applications and restarting VRChat if it sends you back to your home world automatically.\n\nSo, no, this is not a bug. This is just fault of what is being interpreted by the user.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
